.TH OROC-PRINT-BUILD-DIR 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.1.4" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc\-print\-build\-dir \- Print the build directory path
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc print\-build\-dir [\-\-platform=<platform>] [\-\-prod] [\-\-root] [<project\-dir>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Print the build directory path
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-platform\fR
platform to print build directory for (defaults to host):
.br
\(bu android
.br
\(bu android\-emulator
.br
\(bu ios
.br
\(bu ios\-simulator
.TP
\fB\-\-prod\fR
indicate production build directory
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR
print the root build directory
.SH NOTES
.PP
This is useful for scripts that need to locate packaged artifacts, intermediate bundles, or platform\-specific staging directories without reimplementing Oro's path logic.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBoroc print\-build\-dir .\fR
print the host\-platform build directory for the current project
.TP
\fBoroc print\-build\-dir \-\-platform=ios \-\-prod .\fR
print the production iOS build directory
.SH SEE ALSO
oroc(1)
